"""Shared factual contract for existing Shorts role prompts; preserves custom roles."""
from edit_contract import POLICY
CONTRACT='''Content-aware production contract (v6): Follow the CURRENT run brief and saved duration settings, not an older chat topic. Infer the content type from the source evidence. Read the saved director brief and exact event_id. Different distant episodes in a compilation are different stories; use one coherent event and its actual resolution. The visual edit plan may use measured sentence pauses, scene cuts and verified illustrative cutaways while preserving original narration. Comedy needs its real setup and payoff; fashion, music, sport and educational videos need a compelling opening, coherent progression and a supported highlight or closing resolution, not a forced joke. Lyrics are not spoken narration or evidence of a song title, identity or event date. Use humor_type none when appropriate. Use timed transcript or verified visual catalog IDs for edit decisions; candidate plans are alternatives, choose one, never concatenate them. The server checks actual source interval overlap; similar actions at different timestamps are not overlap. Read workspace/PRODUCTION-CONTRACT.md rather than historical setup guides; sparse visual frames prove only their sampled moments. Never fabricate dialogue, timestamps, continuous action, successful tools or quality checks. Preserve the requested source meaning and caption safe area. Edit one understandable story: HOOK at output 0 seconds, then necessary CONTEXT, chronological DEVELOPMENT, a real PAYOFF and a completed ENDING. Infer the topic and causal relationships from the timed transcript, including context_before/context_after; these neighboring lines are evidence, not permission to include unselected footage. A continuation of a cut-off sentence cannot be a hook. Select a self-contained opening line that creates curiosity, preferably brief, without spoiling or falsifying the ending. Finish on an actual completed thought or visual resolution, never a cliff cut mid-sentence. Distinguish statements, questions, answers, negation and quotations. Do not splice separate speakers into a fabricated exchange. In full_content mode preserve the complete source central subject, necessary context and actual outcome through a clearly ordered summary; combine episodes only as an honest summary or compilation, never a fabricated exchange. In single_event mode prefer one coherent source event. Preserve who, what and why, plus the cause of a reaction. Reject or repair unrelated topics even if their timing is valid. Punctuation, pauses and context changes guide cuts; a fixed time window is not a semantic boundary. Do not demand a joke from serious material. Visual evidence governs framing, transcript evidence governs spoken meaning. Label context/development/payoff/ending purposes in beat reasons; choose sound or zoom only where evidence supports the accent. Keep written reasons concise and do not invent dialogue. Captions are 72–80 px at 1080×1920, short readable word groups inside the saved safe box. Publishing belongs only to the verified upload queue when enabled; never claim publication from a draft. Automatic production uses the app's structured stage contracts; your chat response alone does not complete a stage.'''

CONTRACT += '\n'+POLICY+'\nDefault for new productions: FULL SOURCE SUMMARY. Read the complete source before selection, rank all reliable content units, and preserve its main context and actual central outcome. The duration controls what peripheral material is omitted. A coherent summary may span several explicitly separated episodes of the same source; it must not fabricate a conversation or causal sequence. The historical single-incident preference does not override the current full_content scope.'

def upgraded_prompt(prompt):
 import re
 prompt=prompt or ''
 if CONTRACT in prompt:return prompt
 prompt=re.sub(r'\n\nContent-aware production contract \(v\d+\):.*\Z','',prompt,flags=re.S)
 prompt=prompt.replace('90-90 seconds long (1-1.5 minutes)','the duration specified by the current run settings')
 prompt=prompt.replace('No upload or publication is part of local production.','Publication is handled separately by the verified upload queue when enabled.')
 return prompt+'\n\n'+CONTRACT

ROLE_GUIDANCE={
 'transcript':'Preserve original-language words, word times, punctuation, negations, questions and short answers. Mark uncertainty instead of inventing missing speech. Do not rewrite the source into a more dramatic story. Distinguish transcript evidence from visual evidence.',
 'selection':'Read complete neighboring utterances before selecting. Compare real hook candidates, put the chosen hook first, retain required context, build toward a supported payoff and finish a complete thought. Keep independent sentences separately selectable. Open on the actual incident rather than generic banter or a source-channel teaser. Omit promotional filler even from the body. After the hook, preserve chronological cause and reaction. Prefer one coherent event. Produce an evidence-bound storyboard and edit decision list; do not treat sampled windows as story boundaries.',
 'layout':'Use the approved storyboard and timestamped frames. Preserve the game, on-screen demonstration and reaction context. Extra face zoom needs visible evidence; speech alone is insufficient. Do not claim continuous tracking from a few sampled images.',
 'render':'Execute the approved edit decision list exactly. Render 1080x1920 with the saved portrait crop. Use larger 72–80 px timed captions and width-aware short groups in the safe box, no arbitrary camera zoom. Keep source audio continuous across adjacent units and synchronize captions to output time.',
 'verify':'Check the real output and its storyboard: hook begins at output zero, necessary setup remains, a real payoff or visual resolution closes the story, no cut-off speech, accurate captions within safe bounds, no black opening, frozen frame or broken audio. Report the checks actually performed; do not promise virality.'}

def role_prompt(prompt,role):
 import re
 prompt=re.sub(r'\n\nNarrative role \(v\d+\):.*\Z','',prompt or '',flags=re.S)
 result=upgraded_prompt(prompt)
 return result+('\n\nNarrative role (v2): '+ROLE_GUIDANCE[role] if role in ROLE_GUIDANCE else '')
